From 53c9783499d557a612c420313b760e17299345da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: starbite <starbite@local>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:38:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] patch: 0318-port-12377-build-fixes.patch

Compile fixes for xnu-12377 found by the first builds (kept apart from the
patches they touch so later patches' context is not disturbed):
- sleh.c (0004): INTERRUPT_MASKED_DEBUG_START/END became
  ml_interrupt_masked_debug_start/end.
- cpu.c (0065): sysreg_restore is gone (the reset path loads the constant TCR_EL1_BOOT), its PoC clean dropped
- exception.c (0309/0111): the VM map uses range/entry locks now (no vm_map_lock_read/vm_map_lookup_entry); the crash log looks regions up with vm_map_region_recurse_64. vm_kern.c (HEROLTE KMEM log): largest_free_size is now free_size (the kmem range size)
- amcc_rorgn_pv_ctrr.c (0008): new closed-source file in files.arm64 for nos_arm_asm, stubbed like the ppl ones
- exclaves.c, machine_routines.c (0009/0008): tightbeam_startup needs Apple's closed libTightbeam, compiled out for our boards; ml_device_is_prod_fused (closed, new caller in kern_mib.c) answers TRUE
- arm_vm_init.c: progress marks 21-28 between marks 7 and 10 (first 12377 boot stopped after mark 7)
- sweet_early.c, arm_vm_init.c: on the A5XELTE boards the early console stayed off from mark 7 (the 11417 port's assumption), so marks 21-28 never showed; it now stays on until arm_vm_init drops TTBR0 (mark 29), prints two-digit stages, and marks 8/9 bracket the first early_random
- arm_vm_init.c: the dynamic_memory_begin > VM_MAX panic prints the layout on the A5XELTE boards
- MakeInc.def (0093): 12377 selects the layout with ARM64_LARGE_MEMORY (into ARM64_EXTRA_BUILD_FLAGS), LARGE_MEMORY_DEFINE is unused; our boards set ARM64_LARGE_MEMORY = 0 (the first boots panicked: ARM_LARGE_MEMORY physmap below a kernel at 0xfffffff006000000)
- pmap.c: 12377 maps WCOMB/RT pages outside the kernel's DRAM as Device-GRE; on our boards the framebuffer, /pram and Mali buffers are RAM outside it, and bzero's DC ZVA on the Device-mapped panic region faulted in PE_create_console (boot f). WCOMB/RT stay Normal-NC on our boards (pmap_wcomb_normal)
- machine_routines.c: ml_unsafe_kernel_text asserts on iBoot's /chosen kernel-ctrr-to-be-enabled (boot g panicked after dlil_init); our boards have no CTRR and report unlocked text when the property is absent
- vm_map_store.c: VM map guard objects stay off on our boards (launchd faulted with KERN_INVALID_GUARD_OBJECT_SLOT in its first plist buffer, boot h)
- sleh.c: log failing copyio faults on user memory (diagnostic for launchd's KERN_INVALID_GUARD_OBJECT_SLOT exit)
- vm_map_lock.c: log which guard-object check rejects a user range (diagnostic)
- vm_map_lock.c: diagnostic helper moved above its users
- vm_map_store.c: guard objects were still used for user maps (the enable switch only covers the kernel); vm_guard_object_should_fallback now always falls back on our boards, so the fault range of a 4 KiB-kernel/16 KiB-user fault can no longer spill into the next slot
---
